==Strategy==
What makes this stage so difficult and tedious to complete is the lack of assisting enemies for extra money. No matter what strategy you use, at the start of the battle, try and sync all of THE SLOTHs by spamming [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Macho Cat]]. This allows you to stall them easier. Try to not spend more than 15 minutes on this stage, or a trio of assassin bears will appear (but they can still be eliminated with the cat cannon, due to not being buffed). Take note that chipping down the Sloths, the Face and Kurosawah can take a very long time without certain units. In general, [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Gross Cat]] is a huge help in this stage, especially if THE SLOTHs are behind The Face and you manage to stall it.

If you are looking to kill The Face as quickly as possible, cats like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Dancing Flasher Cat]] and [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Butterfly Cat]] can help by doing big damage with few hits.

In higher crown difficulties, you can use the [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]] and [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]] Combos along with [[Mini-Saurus (Combo)|Mini-Saurus]] to spam [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cats]], using the [[Ototo Corps#Breakerblast|Breakerblast Cannon]] to stall the enemies with perfect efficiency while you slowly whittle their health down. [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] helps with this by acting as a wall that the enemies cannot penetrate.

